{"diagnosis": "Trace shows TRAP: no progress max_addr=0x00000000 with tohost FAIL 0xdead vs expected fetch progress. mem_xfer at picorv32.v:373 uses && instead of || so it never asserts without both bus handshake and prefetched word, and mem_done at picorv32.v:376 uses && instead of || so it requires both xfer-path and held-state path. Together they stall the fetch state machine with zero progress, a mut-pair requiring both fixes.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -372,2 +372,2 @@
 	wire mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word = COMPRESSED_ISA && mem_la_firstword && prefetched_high_word && !clear_prefetched_high_word;
-	assign mem_xfer = (mem_valid && mem_ready) && (mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word && mem_do_rinst);
+	assign mem_xfer = (mem_valid && mem_ready) || (mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word && mem_do_rinst);
@@ -375,2 +375,2 @@
 	wire mem_busy = |{mem_do_prefetch, mem_do_rinst, mem_do_rdata, mem_do_wdata};
-	wire mem_done = resetn && ((mem_xfer && |mem_state && (mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata || mem_do_wdata)) && (&mem_state && mem_do_rinst)) &&
+	wire mem_done = resetn && ((mem_xfer && |mem_state && (mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata || mem_do_wdata)) || (&mem_state && mem_do_rinst)) &&
", "expected": "tohost PASS with TRAP cleared and max_addr advancing past 0x00000000"}

